{"slug":"/students/subjects/physics/fluids/bernoulli/","source":"students/subjects/physics/fluids/bernoulli.html","area":"students","kind":"content","title":"Bernoulli's Principle | Physics","description":"","subject":"physics","body":"<div class=\"max-w-4xl mx-auto\">\n    <nav class=\"mb-6\"><a href=\"/students/subjects/physics/fluids/\" class=\"text-blue-600\">← Back to Fluids</a></nav>\n    <article class=\"content-card rounded-xl p-8\">\n      <h1 class=\"text-2xl font-bold mb-2\">Bernoulli's Principle</h1>\n      <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-4\">For steady, incompressible, non-viscous flow: P + ½ρv² + ρgh = constant along a streamline.</p>\n\n      <section class=\"mb-4\">\n        <h2 class=\"font-semibold\">Worked example</h2>\n        <p>Flow speed increases through a constriction; pressure drops — basic lift explanation on airfoils (qualitative).</p>\n      </section>\n\n      <section class=\"mb-4\">\n        <h2 class=\"font-semibold\">Practice</h2>\n        <ol class=\"list-decimal list-inside\">\n          <li>Using Bernoulli, compute pressure difference if speed increases from 2 m/s to 6 m/s in air (ρ≈1.225 kg/m³).</li>\n        </ol>\n      </section>\n\n      <section>\n        <h2 class=\"font-semibold\">Solutions (brief)</h2>\n        <ol class=\"list-decimal list-inside\">\n          <li>ΔP = ½ρ(v2² − v1²) = 0.5×1.225×(36 − 4) ≈ 19.15 Pa.</li>\n        </ol>\n      </section>\n    </article>\n  </div>\n<!-- Topic Quiz System -->","bodyClass":"min-h-screen bg-gradient-to-br from-blue-50 to-indigo-100 p-6","bodyStyle":"","css":["body{font-family:Inter, sans-serif} .content-card{-webkit-backdrop-filter:blur(16px);backdrop-filter:blur(16px);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.2);box-shadow:0 8px 32px rgba(0,0,0,0.06);}"],"quiz":null,"tracker":null,"links":[]}